        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5ed547ab-d119-3970-aabe-37051f9b88fc",
                "word": "exposome",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3f59fd26-91a5-4292-9d92-3baf84005f42",
                        "entry_id": "5ed547ab-d119-3970-aabe-37051f9b88fc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "exposomes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ff7139b9-7ffb-3343-8099-b7a4330dcbc4",
                        "entry_id": "5ed547ab-d119-3970-aabe-37051f9b88fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ensemble des facteurs environnementaux auxquels est exposé un organisme vivant de sa conception à sa mort et qui influencent son état physiologique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Toxicologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e075a6c4-b42d-4b71-bd4a-c3d16f17d7f0",
                                "sense_id": "ff7139b9-7ffb-3343-8099-b7a4330dcbc4",
                                "text": "C’est une loi d’adaptation du système de soin et le volet santé environnementale y est quasi inexistant, à l’exception cependant de la reconnaissance du concept d’« exposome », sans cependant en tirer toutes les conséquences."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48302d52-15c7-4a65-a83e-26b8da0a6f4f",
                                "sense_id": "ff7139b9-7ffb-3343-8099-b7a4330dcbc4",
                                "text": "La découverte et la compréhension de la façon dont cet exposome fonctionne, et ce qu’il induit sur notre santé, sont des domaines de recherche récents, complexes, très pluridisciplinaires."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac2a40c3-9cf2-444a-a355-76e305966d71",
                                "sense_id": "ff7139b9-7ffb-3343-8099-b7a4330dcbc4",
                                "text": "Les recherches sur l’exposome impliquent de croiser de nombreuses disciplines qui relèvent à la fois des sciences « dures » (physique, chimie, science de la terre et de l’environnement, biologie) et des sciences humaines et sociales (anthropologie, sociologie, économie, épidémiologie, santé publique)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2050fef2-baa7-47c0-b3a0-234846801c81",
                        "source_entry_id": "5ed547ab-d119-3970-aabe-37051f9b88fc",
                        "source_sense_id": "ff7139b9-7ffb-3343-8099-b7a4330dcbc4",
                        "target_lang_word": "exposome",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exposome",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba5b4d9a-d7ff-390f-9692-03550c37daed",
                                        "entry_id": "7e1be6bc-76b8-34c8-8be2-c8c4b6419344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A measure of the effects of life-long environmental exposures on health."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a253357-6165-421c-b3d5-964e970b599a",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5b4d9a-d7ff-390f-9692-03550c37daed",
                                                "text": "At its most complete, the exposome encompasses life-course environmental exposures (including lifestyle factors), from the prenatal period onwards."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aec8c896-bd54-495f-a51a-89f099145460",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5b4d9a-d7ff-390f-9692-03550c37daed",
                                                "text": "While the definition of the exposome includes all exposures that occur from conception throughout an individual's lifetime, an emerging concept is the need to also consider exposures prior to conception."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "423b846a-0361-442b-9d68-e379becd0e59",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5b4d9a-d7ff-390f-9692-03550c37daed",
                                                "text": "Every time we pant, or press, or swallow, we welcome into not just our delicate biology but into those cherished fables, too, the ecological influence of the exposome."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c62d52f-6727-4054-a895-af28bf37a5a6",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5b4d9a-d7ff-390f-9692-03550c37daed",
                                                "text": "The exposome is a measure of all the environmental or external exposures we face over our lifetime and the ways in which these impact our health. It includes everything from diet, lifestyle, education and income to air pollution, chemical exposures, and climate conditions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
